# Endings: checked in this order on arrival day; the last one has no conditions.
# Each ending is one carrier clause (the fleet's hail vote) times one arrival clause
# (the storm vote: held the plan, waited it out in orbit, or no storm). Every ending
# closes on the first crate. `title` is the heading; see STORY_BIBLE.md.

card end_lights
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B abort_who
title Lights On
when flag signal_answered
when flag arrive_hold
text In the storm's one pre-dawn slot, the flight director clears one command over the link the handshake opened: lights only. {A} sends it. The dust turns white from below: Cargo 2, spending on every floodlight the charge five days of HOLD let it bank. Eight pilots blind in their plumes check radar against one glow, a floor they can see. {B} sets down closest, well clear. By dawn the glow is one lamp. At noon {B} is at the window when it goes out. The first crate it carried says, in Sharpie: "You'll thank me." To Starbase: "Landed. All eight. The ninth kept the lights on." From a loading bay: "It never could stand being ignored."

card end_through
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B abort_who
title Through the Dust
when flag arrive_hold
text Dust to the windows. Height off the radar, bearing off the knock on two antennas, a fix every eleven seconds till the rim swallows it, then the last metre by feel. The gust catches {B}'s ship: it stands on a folded strut, never to fly home. {B} sits on the bottom rung and lists what it can still be: habitat, store, radio mast. Two sols on, its battery rides a sled up the rim; {A} clips it on, answers inside the tick, then sends the HOLD off the laminated card. One lamp burns steady. {B} adds to the list: neighbour. To Starbase: "Landed. Eight down, seven to fly." From a loading bay: "Tell it the bay says hello."

card end_long_orbit
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B wait_who
title The Long Orbit
when flag signal_answered
when flag arrive_wait
text Week three in the long orbit, half rations. Below the storm one lamp holds steady: the HOLD, holding. Its manifest, tonight: tank liners, a glove, a drill bit. Eight hungry people cheer a drill bit. Next: germination trays, frozen in week two. Its battery kept the lamp or the hold heater, not both; {B} put it to the fleet, and eight hands chose the lamp. {B} logs the trays lost; seven sign under it. On the last night the lamp skips twice; eight galleys hush till it's back. At dawn {B} flies first, calling the numbers for seven. To Starbase: "Landed. All eight. The ninth was waiting." From a loading bay: "Thank it for the drill bit."

card end_patience
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B ow_theory
title Patience
when flag arrive_wait
text Dawn on the rim, frost on the wing. Two weeks of half rations in orbit; all eight came down last night. Past every chart, a battery under that frost has been choosing which knock to skip, and at midnight the flashes stopped. {A} kneels at the service port with a pack, {B} a step behind, counting. Eleven: nothing. Twenty-two: nothing. {A} clips the pack on anyway. Thirty-three: a click, slow, like something clearing its throat. The answer goes in by hand inside the tick, then the HOLD off the laminated card. Its lamp comes on and stays. To Starbase: "Landed. All eight. The ninth is warm." From a loading bay: "Knew it'd keep."

card end_friend
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B ow_theory
title Sit With It
when flag signal_answered
text Second sol, halfway to Cargo 2 for the drill spares. {A} drives; {B} watches the battery: forty-eight percent gone, so they reach it on four, none for the way back. The rule says turn round, unless it charges trucks. The waiver takes eighteen minutes: YOUR CALL. {B} holds up the loading crew's forklift photo. {A} drives on. Cargo 2 hears them and lights the port at its foot. In marker: "Slow charger. Sit with it." All afternoon the charge it kept for the cold runs into the rover. Its lamp is dimmer that night; the cold is closer. To Starbase: "Landed. All eight. The ninth shared its night." From a loading bay: "Slow, not stingy."

card end_close
type ending
cat ending
roles A B
when is A ow_hail
when is B ow_theory
title Close Enough
text Third sol, two hundred metres from Cargo 2. Cargo 3's drill snapped its only bit on the first; the spare is in that hold, and the rover's spares went to heaters on night two. The ruling says spare power in hand; the drill says now. {A} counts the dark, nine, ten, eleven, and answers anyway. HELLO RX · OK. Its patch wakes every heater at once. The HOLD goes out on the next tick. By then it has nothing left to hear it with. {B} puts a glove flat on the cold hull. They drive back heaters off, the bit in {B}'s lap. To Starbase: "Landed. All eight. Found the ninth. In time for the bit." From a loading bay: "Told them. Thank it for us."

